# Methodology

## Project Workflow

The project follows an end-to-end competitive product benchmarking workflow.

### Step 1 — Dataset Collection
A structured dataset was prepared containing product features, competitor information, pricing and performance-related metrics.

### Step 2 — Data Cleaning
The dataset was cleaned by standardizing product names, competitor names, feature categories and availability values.

### Step 3 — Feature Categorization
Features were grouped into categories such as Project Management, Collaboration, Analytics, Automation, AI, Integrations, Security, Mobile, Customization and Customer Support.

### Step 4 — Feature Scoring
Feature availability was converted into a weighted score.

- Yes = 100%
- Partial = 50%
- No = 0%

### Step 5 — KPI Analysis
Key KPIs were calculated to understand overall competitive performance, feature coverage, customer rating, market share and pricing position.

### Step 6 — Competitive Benchmarking
FlowSync was compared against Asana, Monday.com, ClickUp and Notion.

### Step 7 — Gap Analysis
Competitive gaps were identified using competitor score versus FlowSync score.

### Step 8 — Opportunity Prioritization
Opportunities were prioritized using feature gap, customer demand and feature importance.

### Step 9 — Scenario Analysis
Different business scenarios were evaluated to understand possible strategic outcomes.

### Step 10 — Product Roadmap
The highest-priority opportunities were converted into a NOW / NEXT / LATER roadmap.

## Scoring Formula

Feature Gap:

MAX(0, Competitor Score - FlowSync Score)

Opportunity Score:

Feature Gap × Customer Demand × Feature Importance

